# Heading numbering (reference/components/heading.md). Page area of 260 × 260 from (20, 20);
# with FixedMetrics, each character measures 5 pt at Size: 10 and each line, 12.
#
# For element: Document enables Numbered on all the headings and For element: Heading 3 removes it at
# level 3. cover (Numbered: false) is neither numbered nor counted, and In table of contents: false keeps it out of
# the table of contents. The numbers come out as: intro is 1, method 1.1, data 1.2, fine has none (level 3) and
# results is 2.
#
# toc lists levels 1 and 2 (Levels: 1 2): intro, method, data and results, four entries of 12 pt
# (48 in total) and a margin of 8. cover takes up 20..32, toc 32..80, intro starts at 80 + 8 = 88, method
# at 100, data at 112, fine at 124 and ref, which writes "Véase la sección 1.2 y el capítulo 2." (37
# characters, 185 pt, one line), at 136.
#
# results is 95 pt wide (Width: 95, 19 characters). Without a number, "Resultados del año" (18
# characters, 90 pt) would fit on one line; with it, "2 Resultados del año" is 20 characters (100 pt) and
# "año" moves to a second line: results measures 2 × 12 = 24 and starts at 148.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Page:
		Width: 300
		Height: 300
		Margin: 20
	Title: Numeración
	Language: es
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
				Numbered: true
		For element: Heading 3
			Typography:
				Numbered: false
	Section:
		Heading 1:
			Id: cover
			In table of contents: false
			Text: Portada
			Typography:
				Numbered: false
		Table of contents:
			Id: toc
			Levels: 1 2
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 8 0
		Heading 1:
			Id: intro
			Text: Introducción
		Heading 2:
			Id: method
			Text: Método
		Heading 2:
			Id: data
			Text: Datos
		Heading 3:
			Id: fine
			Text: Fino
		Text: Véase la sección {number of: data} y el capítulo {number of: results}.
			Id: ref
		Heading 1:
			Id: results
			Box:
				Width: 95
			Text: Resultados del año
